  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPoint 1 = (7.5, 3.5)\n\nPoint 2 = (2.5, 5.5)\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSlope = (y2 - y1) ÷ (x2 - x1)\n\nEquation: y - y1 = m(x - x1)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ m = (5.5 - 3.5) ÷ (2.5 - 7.5)\n\n⇒ m = 2 ÷ (-5)\n\n⇒ m = -2/5\n\n⇒ y - 3.5 = (-2/5)(x - 7.5)\n\n⇒ y = (-2/5)x + 6.5\n\n⇒ 5y = -2x + 32.5\n\n⇒ 2x + 5y = 32.5\n\n⇒ 4x + 10y = 65\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 4x + 10y = 65.**",
